#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096390 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "a30b523c-d689-520a-a708-f3b5190eaf9d" :question/math-academy-id "e-477" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{1}{1-\\sin^2 x}\\,\\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n\\sin^2 x + \\cos^2 x = 1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad  \\cos^2 x = 1-\\sin^2 x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9934a8da-2378-5019-a3a3-7cd66cbeeaa7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Secant-Tangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "872b9d99-ea39-540f-af2e-acbfa28186b4" :question/math-academy-id "e-478" :question/problem "Calculate $\\, \\displaystyle{\\int} \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we select the identity that contains a $\\tan^2{x}$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+\\tan^2x =\\sec^2x.\n$$\n\nRearranging the above identity gives\n\n$$\n\\tan^2 x =\\sec^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\tan^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\left(\\sec^2 x -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\tan x -x+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0ba6d15-a20e-5f16-b324-0bbead5458ca" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Cosecant-Cotangent Identity"}] :question/id #uuid "d7c09fca-2f4b-5a0a-b687-938527b44d62" :question/math-academy-id "e-479" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int} \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+\\cot^2x =\\csc^2 x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\cot^2 x &=\\csc^2 x -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int \\left(5\\cot^2 x -x^2\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&=\\int \\bigg(5\\left(\\csc^2 x -1 \\right) -x^2\\bigg) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=\\int \\left(5\\csc^2 x -5 -x^2\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n\t\t\t\t&=-5\\cot x -5x-\\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\t\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/id #uuid "14ab2251-66fc-5f94-9821-f14fcc2c03e1" :question/math-academy-id "e-480" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int} 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d} x.$" :question/worked-solution "From the identity  $1+\\tan^2 \\theta =\\sec^2 \\theta$ with $\\theta = 3x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t1+\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x)\\\n\t\t\\tan^2 (3x) &=\\sec^2 (3x) -1.\n}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\int 2\\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\int \\tan^2 (3x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                &= 2\\int \\left(\\sec^2 (3x) -1\\right ) \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\n                                                                 &= 2\\left(\\int \\sec^2 (3x)\\, \\textrm{d}x -\\int1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t                                &= 2\\left( \\dfrac{1}{3}\\tan (3x) -x\\right)+C\\\n                                                                 &= \t\\dfrac{2}{3}\\tan (3x) -2x+C.\n\t}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bace1ab-1f8b-564a-965f-6880a8a258e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bace1ab-1f8b-564a-965f-6880a8a258e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\pi-\\frac{5\\pi^3}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288280} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd544d3-dbff-5f3e-8c77-9b66d9c3f746" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288279}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66b34e07-5d41-5462-a3f4-96722a374f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-346546" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14{cos}^{2}⁡x-5{x}^{2}+14{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14\\cdot 1-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(14-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(14x-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[14\\pi -\\frac{5}{3}{\\pi }^{3}]-[14\\cdot 0-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {0}^{3}] \\\\  & =14\\pi -\\frac{5{\\pi }^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a474c54-9a2c-5453-89fd-c2257bcf7595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a474c54-9a2c-5453-89fd-c2257bcf7595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288297} :answer-field/id #uuid "9298b7c0-47e2-5a26-9926-01bbe7ab3f29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "844ead48-86d3-5441-9336-ed5d8fea3ef1" :question/math-academy-id "q-352714" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the identity $1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x+\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})={sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{1-{cos}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})-[-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-0+1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5822b4-c5d4-59a8-bd72-a41d3074e4e6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Trigonometric Expressions With Linear Arguments Using the Pythagorean Identities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b85f5b77-adcc-5f3a-ac26-aeca80cb6b0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095510} {:answer/id #uuid "270d5846-0eda-5c1b-b012-7d34d46cf1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sec (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095511} {:answer/id #uuid "67d3a24a-4ea6-5077-8ee1-3c6b280ca8e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - 2x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095512} {:answer/id #uuid "734b4c71-0e2a-55b8-a1c5-71df902ee0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095513} {:answer/id #uuid "76de1b0f-7d81-565b-9186-9a8b04d73b39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "734b4c71-0e2a-55b8-a1c5-71df902ee0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\tan (2x + \\frac{π}{6}) - x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095513} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c541591-f947-5bb0-83bf-cb48af5a8cdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095509}] :question/id #uuid "80d349d8-53d5-5ccb-8a77-300f5edef09d" :question/math-academy-id "q-49268" :question/problem "What is $∫\\tan^{2} (2x + \\frac{π}{6})dx$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "19a857ac-d36b-5753-a532-4f2a75612d85" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Pythagorean Trigonometric Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971ad7b9-ca5d-5b66-b8c1-b66d70160833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\cot x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095756} {:answer/id #uuid "97859b41-7974-5d91-af6e-6d2908101b03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x - \\tan x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095757} {:answer/id #uuid "afa0db67-82af-5c4f-81e2-7c47a4774d4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\csc x + \\tan x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095758} {:answer/id #uuid "04c356ed-da2f-57ff-a442-e33763b86966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x - \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095759} {:answer/id #uuid "18275393-75a2-55a2-9dbb-5e9ef87ce4c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x + \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18275393-75a2-55a2-9dbb-5e9ef87ce4c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan x + \\sec x + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095760} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fcad329-096b-5878-ad00-aa6c2af14979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095755}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "549e92f3-8254-599c-8f33-a7787db1bdf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-51122" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We use a variation of the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\\,⟹\\,{cos}^{2}⁡x=1-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the denominator and calculate the resulting integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
